# Docker build context guard for web-dashboard.
#
# The web-dashboard repo co-locates a Next.js frontend with a Python FastAPI
# backend (backend/, the 8os Orchestrator). The frontend is the deployed
# service; the backend is its own separate Railway service.
#
# The top-level Dockerfile builds Next.js standalone. Excluding backend/ from
# the Docker build context keeps the FastAPI source out of the Next.js image
# (no wasted layer, no accidental presence) and makes the build deterministic
# regardless of builder config. This is a hardening measure for OS-4615
# (RAILPACK drift recurrence on 2026-07-24) following OS-4324 (RAILPACK drift
# on 2026-07-21).

# Never ship the FastAPI orchestrator inside the Next.js image.
backend/
backend/**

# Local development + repo hygiene (most already .gitignored, but be explicit
# at the build context level so a fresh clone without git history still
# builds cleanly).
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright/.cache/
coverage/
.vercel/
.railway/
.turbo/
.env
.env*
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.sqlite
*.swp
*.swo
